[
  {
    "directory": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071101",
    "question": {
      "math_academy_id": "q-83641",
      "knowledge_point_id": "8c3fc090-22e5-5f05-9634-b8c645cf5700",
      "knowledge_point": "Calculating the Expected Value Given the Frequency of a Random Variable",
      "problem": "Several egg cartons were checked for cracked eggs. The number of cracked eggs in each carton was recorded below. If $N$ is the number of cracked eggs in a carton, what is the expected value of $N?$\n\n| Number of Cartons | $10$ | $7$ | $2$ | $1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Cracked Eggs | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |",
      "worked_solution": "The expected value of a discrete random variable $X$ with probability mass function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]={\\sum }_{x\\in S}x\\cdot f(x).\n$$\n\nWe're given the frequencies of the cracked eggs, so we can start by computing the corresponding probabilities. The total number of cartons is $10+7+2+1=20,$ so the corresponding probabilities are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(N=0)=f(0) & =\\frac{10}{20}=\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ P(N=1)=f(1) & =\\frac{7}{20} \\\\ P(N=2)=f(2) & =\\frac{2}{20}=\\frac{1}{10} \\\\ P(N=3)=f(3) & =\\frac{1}{20}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe organize these results in the table below.\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\frac{7}{20}$ | $\\frac{1}{10}$ | $\\frac{1}{20}$ |\n\nNow, summing up the products of each value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[N] & =0\\cdot f(0)+1\\cdot f(1)+2\\cdot f(2)+3\\cdot f(3) \\\\  & =0(\\frac{1}{2})+1(\\frac{7}{20})+2(\\frac{1}{10})+3(\\frac{1}{20}) \\\\  & =0+\\frac{7}{20}+\\frac{2}{10}+\\frac{3}{20} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{20}+\\frac{4}{20}+\\frac{3}{20} \\\\  & =\\frac{7+4+3}{20} \\\\  & =\\frac{14}{20} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{10} \\\\  & =0.7.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "answer_fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices_complete": true,
          "choices": [
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "0.7",
              "option": "0",
              "source_option": "a"
