  {
    "directory": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071102",
    "question": {
      "math_academy_id": "q-79697",
      "knowledge_point_id": "7de671ee-7bba-54ce-bec2-d2d6f5569f4a",
      "knowledge_point": "Writing First-Order Linear ODEs in Standard Form",
      "problem": "Write the following first-order linear ODE in standard form.\n\n$$\n(\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}})\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{x+y}{x}\\,.\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "A first order linear ODE is in standard form if it is written as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x)\\,,\n$$\n\nwhere $P(x)$ and $Q(x)$ do not depend on $y.$\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nWe have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}})\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{x+y}{x} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={x}^{2}(\\frac{x+y}{x}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =x(x+y) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={x}^{2}+xy \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,+{{(-x)}_{⏟}}_{P(x)}y & ={{{x}^{2}}_{⏟}}_{Q(x)} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-xy & ={x}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the equation is written in standard form with $P(x)=-x$ and $Q(x)={x}^{2}.$",
      "answer_fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices_complete": true,
          "choices": [
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-(1+x)y=0",
              "option": "0",
              "source_option": "a"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-xy={x}^{2}",
              "option": "1",
              "source_option": "b"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+xy=\\frac{1}{x}",
              "option": "2",
              "source_option": "c"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-y=-{x}^{2}",
              "option": "3",
              "source_option": "d"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-xy=2x",
              "option": "4",
              "source_option": "e"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "difficulty": "easy",
      "provenance": {
        "activity_question": "question-79697",
        "kp_title": "Writing First-Order Linear ODEs in Standard Form",
