  {
    "directory": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071103",
    "question": {
      "math_academy_id": "q-75732",
      "knowledge_point_id": "49c501da-161c-53be-8349-571cc6a07975",
      "knowledge_point": "Plotting the Product of a Matrix and an Eigenvector Given its Corresponding Eigenvalue",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071103/assets/312c7d003e2d856e55b3b5700402aa86b53e43dcd8f8650b4e04476b8be9b585.png)\n\nThe vector $v$ is an eigenvector of a $2\\times 2$ matrix $C$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $-2.$ Find the vector $Cv.$",
      "worked_solution": "The eigenvector $v=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]$ corresponds to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =-2.$ So, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Cv & =-2v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have the following picture:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071103/assets/1ef0448df9f0a37289e9792ce62e6c92203aeb4333f2b25f21c608b5253cf1fe.png)",
      "answer_fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices_complete": true,
          "choices": [
