  {
    "directory": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071103",
    "question": {
      "math_academy_id": "q-75735",
      "knowledge_point_id": "49c501da-161c-53be-8349-571cc6a07975",
      "knowledge_point": "Plotting the Product of a Matrix and an Eigenvector Given its Corresponding Eigenvalue",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071103/assets/61ed37aa6a5e67cdc60cca2c93969a47d12e1e36f18edf96f646922877641e79.png)\n\nThe vector $u$ is an eigenvector of a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\frac{1}{2}.$ Find the vector $Au.$",
      "worked_solution": "The eigenvector $u=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$ corresponds to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =\\frac{1}{2}.$ So, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Au & =\\frac{1}{2}u.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we have the following picture:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071103/assets/c272ff1454ac4ab9825e312f563c9bca08ac2800faa0e95ab45e8a5e827369da.png)",
