  {
    "directory": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071291",
    "question": {
      "math_academy_id": "q-77547",
      "knowledge_point_id": "2b677c92-5390-5cd1-b1d3-b84d180c2b3e",
      "knowledge_point": "Calculating the Complex Conjugate of a Complex Vector",
      "problem": "Given the vectors ${x}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}3-8\\text{i} \\\\ -4+2\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]$ and ${x}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-6\\text{i} \\\\ 1+2\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]$, then ${x}_{1}+\\text{i}\\cdot {\\overset{―}{x}}_{2}=$",
      "worked_solution": "To find the complex conjugate of a vector, we take the complex conjugate of the entries of the vector. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\overset{―}{x}}_{2} & =\\overset{―}{[\\begin{aligned}-6\\text{i} \\\\ 1+2\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{-6\\text{i}} \\\\ \\overset{―}{1+2\\text{i}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}6\\text{i} \\\\ 1-2\\text{i}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying the second vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{i}\\cdot {\\overset{―}{x}}_{2} & =\\text{i}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}6\\text{i} \\\\ 1-2\\text{i}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}6{\\text{i}}^{2} \\\\ \\text{i}-2{\\text{i}}^{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 2+\\text{i}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+\\text{i}\\cdot {\\overset{―}{x}}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}3-8\\text{i} \\\\ -4+2\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 2+\\text{i}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3-8\\text{i} \\\\ -2+3\\text{i}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "answer_fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices_complete": true,
          "choices": [
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "[\\begin{aligned}-3-8\\text{i} \\\\ -2+3\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]",
