    "question": {
      "math_academy_id": "q-130890",
      "knowledge_point_id": "689f9f44-4776-56a7-915f-d0dab0755002",
      "knowledge_point": "Computing Components of the Real and Imaginary Parts of a Complex Vector",
      "problem": "If $\\,\\text{Re}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ b\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,\\text{Im}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}c \\\\ d\\end{aligned}]\\,$ are the real and imaginary parts of the vector $\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}1-3\\text{i} \\\\ -1-5\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]\\,$ then what is the value of $ac+bd?$",
      "worked_solution": "For the given vector $\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}1-3\\text{i} \\\\ -1-5\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]\\,$ we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =[\\begin{aligned}1-3\\text{i} \\\\ -1-5\\text{i}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{\\text{Re}(x)}+\\text{i}{{[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{\\text{Im}(x)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore $\\,a=1,b=-1,c=-3$ and $d=-5$, which implies that \n\n$$\nac+bd=1\\cdot (-3)+(-1)\\cdot (-5)=2.\n$$",
      "answer_fields": [
