      "knowledge_point": "Computing Components of the Real and Imaginary Parts of a Complex Vector",
      "problem": "If $\\,\\text{Re}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ b\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,\\text{Im}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}c \\\\ d\\end{aligned}]\\,$ are the real and imaginary parts of the vector $\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}-6+7\\text{i} \\\\ 1-6\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]\\,$ then what is the value of $ad+bc?$",
      "worked_solution": "For the given vector $\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}-6+7\\text{i} \\\\ 1-6\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]\\,$ we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =[\\begin{aligned}-6+7\\text{i} \\\\ 1-6\\text{i}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{\\text{Re}(x)}+\\text{i}\\,{{[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{\\text{Im}(x)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore $\\,a=-6,b=1,c=7$ and $d=-6$, which implies that \n\n$$\nad+bc=(-6)\\cdot (-6)+1\\cdot 7=43.\n$$",
